Relevant columns and their typical usage for this task  
• `posts_questions.title`: text of the question – use it to find titles that start with or contain the word “how”.  
• `posts_questions.tags`: angle‑bracket delimited list of tags – use it to restrict the search to Android–related tags (e.g. `<android-layout>`).  
• `posts_questions.view_count`: number of times the question has been viewed – use it to determine “most viewed”.  

Typical conditions you will combine  
1. `LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'` – pick titles that begin with “how ”.  
2. `REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags, r'<android-layout>|<android-activity>|<android-intent>|<android>|<android-fragment>')` – keep rows whose tag list contains at least one of the desired Android tags.  

Below are ten exploratory → increasingly focused queries (all limited to 20 rows except the final one) showing how you could work toward the answer.  Replace / extend the tag list if you need more tags.

```sql
-- 1) Peek at the structure of android questions
SELECT id, title, tags, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags, r'<android>')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) See distinct android‑related tags that appear the most
SELECT tag, COUNT(*) AS cnt
FROM (
  SELECT SPLIT(REGEXP_REPLACE(tags, '[<>]', ''), '><') AS tag_arr
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
  WHERE REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags, r'<android')
), UNNEST(tag_arr) AS tag
GROUP BY tag
ORDER BY cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Sample “how …” questions, whatever the topic
SELECT id, title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
ORDER BY creation_date DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Combine “how …” with one android tag: android-layout
SELECT id, title, tags, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags, r'<android-layout>')
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Same, android-activity
SELECT id, title, tags, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags, r'<android-activity>')
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Cover three tags at once (layout, activity, intent)
SELECT id, title, tags, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags,
        r'<android-layout>|<android-activity>|<android-intent>')
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Inspect the top‑viewed android “how” questions regardless of tag
SELECT id, title, tags, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags, r'<android')
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) For the chosen tag list, show the max view_count you will need
SELECT MAX(view_count) AS max_views
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags,
        r'<android-layout>|<android-activity>|<android-intent>|<android>|<android-fragment>');
```

```sql
-- 9) Double‑check that exactly one question owns that max view count
SELECT title, view_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags,
        r'<android-layout>|<android-activity>|<android-intent>|<android>|<android-fragment>')
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL: title of the single most viewed “how …” android question
SELECT title
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE LOWER(title) LIKE 'how %'
  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(tags,
        r'<android-layout>|<android-activity>|<android-intent>|<android>|<android-fragment>')
ORDER BY view_count DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

